<item><title>Algeria&apos;s state news agency alleges France offered asylum for testimony against Algeria</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-s-state-news-agency-alleges-france-offered-asylum-bdab9d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dz/algeria-s-state-news-agency-alleges-france-offered-asylum-bdab9d/</guid><category>Algeria</category><description>The Algerian Press Service (APS), the state news agency, says consular agent Smaïl R. has been held in France for 596 days without valid reason.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:00:21 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dz.jpg" length="32980" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dz.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
